364: -- Pure function of the two rows; null = allowed, otherwise the reason.
365: -- Mirrors the TypeScript rule: different (non-null) companies deny; with an
366: -- access_control object, a non-empty allowedUsers must contain users.id, a
367: -- non-empty allowedRoles must contain the user's role, and a room that is not
368: -- public (JavaScript truthiness of isPublic) with no allowed users/roles
369: -- denies a user without a company; a falsy access_control (null, false, 0,
370: -- "") skips the access-control checks, as in TypeScript. Stricter than the
371: -- TypeScript rule only for malformed data, which denies (ROOM_ACL_INVALID): an
