104:  * someone else, once its conversation is known. Only live Realtime events
105:  * reach it — never the catch-up/refetch/polling paths. Realtime can still
106:  * deliver, as a live event, a message committed shortly before this page
107:  * subscribed (it matches changes when it reads them from the WAL, which can
108:  * lag behind the commit), so a message already covered by the first
109:  * conversation list this page loaded is not announced either: messages that
110:  * already existed are never announced (TRACK T31).
111:  *
112:  * Phase 5 T18 (FR-025, BR-011): a direct/group message, or a room message
113:  * that mentions the user, is authorized by the server under the browser's
114:  * session (member; for rooms, mentioned), the session is confirmed to be this
115:  * user's, and only then claimed once per browser (Phase 4 claim; block C fix
116:  * F4). Then, with no await before display, it is dropped if the signed-in
117:  * user changed, a "Sair mesmo" stop began, a removal from the conversation
118:  * was received (its list-stream event since the message arrived, F1; it left
119:  * the cached list, or its roster read 403), notifications were turned
120:  * off, or any visible tab of the user in this browser shows the
121:  * conversation. A message that mentions the user is announced as a mention
122:  * — never also as an ordinary message.
123:  */
