1: -- Phase 2.3 (messaging audit 2026-06-10, S-05): RLS membership source moves
2: -- from conversations.participants[] to conversation_members.
3: --
4: -- conversation_members is kept in sync with participants[] by the
5: -- trigger_sync_conversation_members trigger (20260610210000), so this is a
6: -- semantic no-op today; it makes conversation_members the single membership
7: -- authority so participants[] can be dropped in Phase 3.
8: --
9: -- Exception kept on participants[]: the conversations INSERT policy. Member
10: -- rows are created by an AFTER INSERT trigger, so at WITH CHECK time the
11: -- membership rows do not exist yet — the check must read NEW.participants.
12: --
13: -- Also tightens X-02 while touching messages RLS: update_own_messages gains a
14: -- WITH CHECK so a sender cannot rewrite a message into a conversation they are
15: -- not a member of (full old-vs-new column comparison is not expressible in RLS).
16: --
17: -- Re-runnable: every policy is dropped and recreated; the helper is
18: -- CREATE OR REPLACE.
19: 
20: -- ============================================================================
21: -- 1) Membership helper. SECURITY DEFINER so it reads conversation_members
22: --    regardless of that table's own RLS (and stays usable inside realtime WAL
23: --    RLS evaluation). private schema is not exposed via PostgREST.
24: -- ============================================================================
