587: State delta (client-only; no route, repository, DB or migration change):
588: - F1 (#1): `claimOldestOutboxItem` strict durability (outbox-db.ts:339, :416); later relaxed writes leave the 
item claimed → fenced.
589: - F2 (#2): `hold()` clears this owner's pending views; render/showItem empty while held, restored by 
`verifyOwner`→`loadAll`. `enqueue` checks identity first: `other`/`ended` → `OutboxNotOwnerError`, composer keeps the 
draft (generic send error text); `unverified` still queues (offline with expired token). Sign-out count and purge take 
an `isOwner` check (outbox-sign-out.ts:78, :125, 3 s bound): not owner → count 0, purge deletes nothing; purge 
re-checks at confirm. useMessageOutbox builds the identity once per ownerAuthUid.
590: - F3 (#3): observing a stored key whose row holds a live claim marks the row `retired: true` and keeps 
claim/lease; the claim transaction deletes a retired row once its claim may end and takes the next item; retired rows 
hidden and excluded from the sign-out count; new optional `retired` in types/message-outbox.ts.
591: - F4 (#4 cheap parts): claim takes `ClaimTakeover {acquiredAt, stolen}` and returns `busy` instead of replacing a 
live foreign claim when the lock was stolen or the claim was made at/after this drain got the lock; a live claim older 
than the lock acquisition (closed/crashed tab) is still taken over. `mayDispatch` re-checks disposed/held/sign-out 
stop/lost lock after the awaited owner verification. Confirmed deletes skip a row claimed by another holder at a newer 
generation.
592: - F5-partial (#5): `fenceThenAttempt` checks `mayDispatch` right before the create.
593: - F8 (#8): delivered with a null message (fence stored/null, create 410) is broadcast `{delivered, deleted: 
true}`; receivers drop their kept copy.
